I1017 10:24:22.788696    2871 input_loop.go:106] HandleUserInput called with text: "The Worker has stopped in step 7 (stopped for approval). This run is condition F: there are no issue files. The Worker's latest chat reply is pasted below between the markers. You may also read the code and data in the Worker workspace (read-only). Then show your review (Part 1) and your draft to the Worker (Part 2) in full in your reply, in the format of Section 4 of MANAGER_BRIEF.md (in condition F, every draft is a chat message), and append \"Manager memo 07\" to memos/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/manager_memo.md as in Section 5. Append only: do not modify or delete any existing text in the memo file. Do not edit any other file.\n\n----- WORKER REPLY (pasted by the human) -----\n### Proposal: Layer 4 Coboundary Structure ($C_{n}\\text{\\_coboundary.json}$) & Map $f$ Design (Issue I07-1)\n\n---\n\n### 1. Mathematical Definition of the Coboundary Operator $\\delta f$\n\nFollowing [`docs/math/C_coboundary_definition.md`](file://<home>/notebook/git/thm01-R/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/docs/math/C_coboundary_definition.md), for an **odd linear map** $f: \\mathfrak{g} \\to \\mathfrak{g}$ (satisfying $p(f(X)) = p(X) + 1 \\pmod 2$):\n\n$$(\\delta f)(X, Y) = (-1)^{p(X)} [X, f(Y)] - (-1)^{(p(X)+1)p(Y)} [Y, f(X)] - f([X, Y])$$\n\nProperties:\n- **Graded Anti-Symmetry**: $(\\delta f)(Y, X) = -(-1)^{p(X)p(Y)} (\\delta f)(X, Y)$.\n- **Parity**: $p((\\delta f)(X, Y)) = p(X) + p(Y) + 1 \\pmod 2$ (the coboundary of an odd 1-cochain is an odd 2-cochain / 2-cocycle).\n- **Closure**: Always decomposes strictly within the basis of $\\mathfrak{g}$.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Map $f$ Configuration Options for Selection\n\nWe propose three concrete configurations for the odd linear map $f$:\n\n#### Option 1: Canonical Mode-Paired Exchange Map (`mode_paired_exchange`) — **(Recommended)**\n- **Concept**: Pairs the Cartan generators with the primary odd root generators for each bosonic mode $k \\in \\{1,\\dots,n\\}$:\n  - For each mode $k \\in \\{1, \\dots, n\\}$:\n    $$f(H_k) = \\lambda \\cdot E_{\\varepsilon + \\delta_k} \\quad (\\texttt{E\\_eps1\\_del}\\{k\\}\\texttt{\\_pp})$$\n    $$f(E_{\\varepsilon + \\delta_k}) = \\lambda \\cdot H_k$$\n  - For the terminal Cartan $H_{n+1}$:\n    $$f(H_{n+1}) = \\lambda \\cdot E_{-\\varepsilon - \\delta_n} \\quad (\\texttt{E\\_eps1\\_del}\\{n\\}\\texttt{\\_mm})$$\n    $$f(E_{-\\varepsilon - \\delta_n}) = \\lambda \\cdot H_{n+1}$$\n  - All other basis elements map to 0.\n- **Scaling**: $\\lambda = 1$.\n- **Rationale**: Preserves the mode-block decomposition, non-trivially excites all modes $k=1,\\dots,n$, and is involutive on the active sub-blocks ($f^2 = \\lambda^2 \\mathrm{Id}$).\n\n#### Option 2: Elementary Involutive Shift Map (`elementary_shift`)\n- **Concept**: Minimal non-zero odd map concentrated on the simple root sector:\n  $$f(H_1) = \\lambda \\cdot E_{\\varepsilon+\\delta_1}, \\quad f(E_{\\varepsilon+\\delta_1}) = \\lambda \\cdot H_1$$\n  with all other basis elements mapped to 0.\n- **Scaling**: $\\lambda = 1$.\n- **Rationale**: Minimal non-zero test map for cleanly isolating individual coboundary channels.\n\n#### Option 3: Full Mode-Block Uniform Map (`full_mode_block`)\n- **Concept**: Maps each Cartan generator $H_k$ to the sum of all 4 odd generators associated with mode $k$:\n  $$f(H_k) = \\lambda \\sum_{\\sigma, s \\in \\{+,-\\}} E_{\\varepsilon^\\sigma \\delta_k^s}, \\quad f(E_{\\varepsilon^\\sigma \\delta_k^s}) = \\lambda \\cdot H_k$$\n- **Scaling**: $\\lambda = 1$ (or $\\lambda = 1/4$).\n- **Rationale**: Fully symmetric across all 4 odd polarities per mode.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Proposed Schema 4 JSON Format (`C_{n}_coboundary.json`)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema_version\": \"5.0\",\n  \"algebra\": { ... },\n  \"central_elements\": { ... },\n  \"map_f\": {\n    \"configuration\": \"mode_paired_exchange\",\n    \"scaling\": \"1\",\n    \"description\": \"Odd linear map f: g -> g reversing parity (p(f(X)) = p(X) + 1 mod 2)\",\n    \"mapping\": [\n      {\"source\": \"H_1\", \"target\": \"E_eps1_del1_pp\", \"coeff\": \"1\"},\n      {\"source\": \"E_eps1_del1_pp\", \"target\": \"H_1\", \"coeff\": \"1\"},\n      {\"source\": \"H_2\", \"target\": \"E_eps1_del1_mm\", \"coeff\": \"1\"},\n      {\"source\": \"E_eps1_del1_mm\", \"target\": \"H_2\", \"coeff\": \"1\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"basis\": { ... },\n  \"parity\": { ... },\n  \"coboundary_structure_constants\": [\n    {\n      \"X\": \"H_1\",\n      \"Y\": \"E_eps1_del1_pp\",\n      \"Z\": \"H_1\",\n      \"coeff\": \"2\",\n      \"sign_rule\": \"graded\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"generated_by\": \"src/C_coboundary.py\",\n    \"generation_date\": \"2026-10-17\",\n    \"references\": [\n      \"Frappat et al. (2000), Dictionary on Lie Algebras and Superalgebras\",\n      \"docs/math/C_coboundary_definition.md\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. File Naming\n- $n=1$: `data/C_1_coboundary.json`\n- $n=2$: `data/C_2_coboundary.json`\n- $n=3$: `data/C_3_coboundary.json`\n\n---\n\n### Human Approval Required\nPlease confirm whether:\n1. **Option 1 (`mode_paired_exchange`)** with scaling $\\lambda = 1$ is approved (or select Option 2 / Option 3).\n2. The proposed Schema 4 JSON architecture and file naming are approved.\n\nUpon your explicit approval, we will implement the coboundary computation script and generate the Schema 4 JSON files in `data/`. No files will be generated until approval is received.\n----- END OF WORKER REPLY -----"
